    },
    {
      "text": "(6)",
      "bbox": [
        526.0797119140625,
        399.0533752441406,
        539.9024047851562,
        411.20611572265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where v ∼N(0, d2) with standard deviation d = diag([1, 0.1, 0.05, 1, 0.1, 0.05]). The friction coeﬃ-",
      "bbox": [
        71.99972534179688,
        456.0212097167969,
        539.885009765625,
        468.6858215332031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cient is µ = 10−4. The state components x1, x2, x3 are the position, velocity, and hidden state of the",
      "bbox": [
        71.99905395507812,
        469.101318359375,
        539.8423461914062,
        483.4460144042969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lead vehicle, while the components x4, x5, x6 are the position, velocity, and hidden state of the ego",
      "bbox": [
        71.99894714355469,
        482.8132019042969,
        539.8414916992188,
        496.6460266113281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "vehicle. The surrogate model is a neural network with ReLU activation functions and with layers",
      "bbox": [
        71.99923706054688,
        495.893310546875,
        539.7982788085938,
        508.0460510253906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[6, 32, 32, 32, 6]. The surrogate model is trained from a training dataset generated from Eq. (6) where",
      "bbox": [
        71.99923706054688,
        509.09332275390625,
        539.8954467773438,
        521.24609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the control input u is generated by the adaptive cruise controller. To perform conformal inference,",
      "bbox": [
        71.99923706054688,
        522.1734008789062,
        539.86767578125,
        534.326171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we generate L = 40000 i.i.d. 50-step trajectories from Eq. (6) with sampling time δt = 0.1 sec that",
      "bbox": [
        71.99957275390625,
        535.3734130859375,
        539.8980712890625,
        547.5261840820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we collect within the test dataset Dtest. Fig. 1 shows the projections of our probabilistic ﬂowpipe",
      "bbox": [
        71.99929809570312,
        548.4535522460938,
        539.8215942382812,
        560.6063232421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "onto its state components by setting ε = 0.01. To visualize the tightness of the probabilistic ﬂow-",
      "bbox": [
        71.99948120117188,
        561.6535034179688,
        539.8356323242188,
        573.8062744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pipe, we generate 100000 additional i.i.d. trajectories from Eq. (6) and include their projection on",
      "bbox": [
        71.99942016601562,
        574.7332153320312,
        540.0091552734375,
        586.885986328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "their state components in Fig. 1 as well. Table 1 shows the run time of our experimental results for",
      "bbox": [
        71.99911499023438,
        587.9332275390625,
        539.990966796875,
        600.0859985351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the range ε ∈[0.01, 0.1].",
      "bbox": [
        71.99911499023438,
        601.0133056640625,
        185.4095458984375,
        613.1660766601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Quadcopter. We consider a 12-dimensional Quadcopter model that was introduced in [6]. The ODE",
      "bbox": [
        71.9986343383789,
        619.6133422851562,
        539.8947143554688,
        631.76611328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model for the Quadcopter is shown in Eq. (7). The additive noise v = [v1, v2, · · · , v12] is Gaussian",
      "bbox": [
        71.99951171875,
        632.8132934570312,
        539.9976196289062,
        645.9114379882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "v ∼N(0, d2) with standard deviation d = diag([0.05 ×⃗11×6, 0.01 ×⃗11×6]). The controller is a",
      "bbox": [
        71.99978637695312,
        645.381103515625,
        540.0007934570312,
        658.9915161132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "neural network controller that was presented in [6]. From this model, we generate a test dataset",
      "bbox": [
        71.99972534179688,
        659.0933837890625,
        539.8704833984375,
        671.2461547851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "with L = 40000 data-points by sampling 50-step trajectories with sampling time δt = 0.1 sec. We",
      "bbox": [
        71.99972534179688,
        672.1735229492188,
        540.014892578125,
        684.3262939453125
      ],
      "direction": [
